ite after a deploy is expensive.** The first policy write extended the contract's storage lifetime and charged 368.39 test XLM in fees (transaction cb406cd0…); a simulated policy write now costs about 1 XLM."},"330":{"id":"/security/limits-and-known-risks-9","page_id":"/security/limits-and-known-risks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/security/limits-and-known-risks","content":"**Agent keys are hot keys.** A leaked key can use the spending authority its policy permits until the policy is paused, removed or expires."},"331":{"id":"/security/limits-and-known-risks-10","page_id":"/security/limits-and-known-risks","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/security/limits-and-known-risks","content":"Sources: `packages/app/src/chain/testnet.ts` (`events`); `packages/sdk/src/worker.ts`; `contracts/team-account/src/lib.rs`; `deployments/testnet.json`."},"332":{"id":"/security/security-model","page_id":"/security/security-model","type":"page","content":"Security model","breadcrumbs":["EcoRouter Docs","Security"],"tags":[],"url":"/security/security-model"},"333":{"id":"/security/security-model-0","page_id":"/security/security-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/security/security-model","content":"The team-account contract checks each payment and remains the source of authorization."},"334":{"id":"/security/security-model-1","page_id":"/security/security-model","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/security/security-model#payment-check-order","content":"Payment check order"},"335":{"id":"/security/security-model-2","page_id":"/security/security-model","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/security/security-model#transaction-authorization","content":"Transaction authorization"},"336":{"id":"/security/security-model-3","page_id":"/security/security-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/security/security-model","content":"EcoRouter is **Stellar testnet only** and is **not audited**. Use test funds."},"337":{"id":"/security/security-model-4","page_id":"/security/security-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/security/security-model","content":"The app and SDK can simulate `check` before submission, but a client-side result is not authorization. The Soroban `team-account` contract holds the funds and enforces policy during `pay(spender, service, amount, memo, key)`."},"338":{"id":"/security/security-model-5","page_id":"/security/security-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/security/security-model#payment-check-order","content":"Account is not paused."},"339":{"id":"/security/security-model-6","page_id":"/security/security-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/security/security-model#payment-check-order","content":"Spender has a policy."},"340":{"id":"/security/security-model-7","page_id":"/security/security-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/security/security-model#payment-check-order","content":"Spender is not paused."},"341":{"id":"/security/security-model-8","page_id":"/security/security-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/security/security-model#payment-check-order","content":"Policy has not expired."},"342":{"id":"/security/security-model-9","page_id":"/security/security-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/security/security-model#payment-check-order","content":"Amount is positive."},"343":{"id":"/security/security-model-10","page_id":"/security/security-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/security/security-model#payment-check-order","content":"Service is on the spender's list."},"344":{"id":"/security/security-model-11","page_id":"/security/security-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/security/security-model#payment-check-order","content":"Replay key has not been used."},"345":{"id":"/security/security-model-12","page_id":"/security/security-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/security/security-model#payment-check-order","content":"Amount does not exceed the per-payment cap."},"346":{"id":"/security/security-model-13","page_id":"/security/security-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/security/security-model#payment-check-order","content":"Payment count is within the period limit."},"347":{"id":"/security/security-model-14","page_id":"/security/security-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/security/security-model#payment-check-order","content":"Amount fits the allowance remaining."},"348":{"id":"/security/security-model-15","page_id":"/security/security-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/security/security-model#payment-check-order","content":"Registry resolves the service and it is active."},"349":{"id":"/security/security-model-16","page_id":"/security/security-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/security/security-model#payment-check-order","content":"Team-account balance covers the transfer."},"350":{"id":"/security/security-model-17","page_id":"/security/security-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/security/security-model#payment-check-order","content":"USDC is transferred and a receipt event is emitted."},"351":{"id":"/security/security-model-18","page_id":"/security/security-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/security/security-model#payment-check-order","content":"The first failed check stops the call. A person can request approval for the service allowlist, payment cap, payment count or allowance rules. An agent cannot request an exception. The code and ordering are in `contracts/team-account/src/lib.rs`; user-facing titles are in `packages/app/src/engine/rules.ts`."},"352":{"id":"/security/security-model-19","page_id":"/security/security-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/security/security-model#transaction-authorization","content":"The spender authorizes its own payment. The contract resolves the payee from `service-registry`; callers cannot supply a raw recipient address. A 32-byte key is stored when a payment succeeds, and `is_key_used` reports whether it has already been used."},"353":{"id":"/security/security-model-20","page_id":"/security/security-model","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/security/security-model#transaction-authorization","content":"Sources: `contracts/team-account/src/lib.rs` (`check`, `pay`, `is_key_used`); `contracts/service-registry/src/lib.rs` (`resolve`)."},"354":{"id":"/using/activity-and-receipts","page_id":"/using/activity-and-receipts","type":"page","content":"Receipts","breadcrumbs":["EcoRouter Docs","Using EcoRouter"],"tags":[],"url":"/using/activity-and-receipts"},"355":{"id":"/using/activity-and-receipts-0","page_id":"/using/activity-and-receipts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/using/activity-and-receipts","content":"Every payment attempt leaves a receipt in Activity."},"356":{"id":"/using/activity-and-receipts-1","page_id":"/using/activity-and-receipts","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/using/activity-and-receipts#outcomes","content":"Outcomes"},"357":{"id":"/using/activity-and-receipts-2","page_id":"/using/activity-and-receipts","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/using/activity-and-receipts#on-chain","content":"On chain"},"358":{"id":"/using/activity-and-receipts-3","page_id":"/using/activity-and-receipts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/using/activity-and-receipts","content":"The **Activity** screen lists every payment attempt as a receipt. A receipt records who paid (the spender), the service id, the amount, the memo, the time, and the outcome."},"359":{"id":"/using/activity-and-receipts-4","page_id":"/using/activity-and-receipts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/using/activity-and-receipts#outcomes","content":"| Outcome     | Meaning                                                  | Money moved |\n| ----------- | -------------------------------------------------------- | ----------- |\n| **Settled** | Every check passed and USDC went to the service's payee. | Yes         |","table":"table-0"},"360":{"id":"/using/activity-and-receipts-5","page_id":"/using/activity-and-receipts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/using/activity-and-receipts#outcomes","content":"| Outcome  | Meaning                                                        | Money moved |\n| -------- | -------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------- |\n| **Held** | A limit caught the payment. It may become an approval request. | No          |","table":"table-0"},"361":{"id":"/using/activity-and-receipts-6","page_id":"/using/activity-and-receipts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/using/activity-and-receipts#outcomes","content":"| Outcome      | Meaning                                 | Money moved |\n| ------------ | --------------------------------------- | ----------- |\n| **Declined** | The owner declined an approval request. | No          |","table":"table-0"},"362":{"id":"/using/activity-and-receipts-7","page_id":"/using/activity-and-receipts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/using/activity-and-receipts#outcomes","content":"| Outcome     | Meaning                                                          | Money moved |\n| ----------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------- |\n| **Refused** | A check that cannot be approved failed, or an agent hit a limit. | No          |","table":"table-0"},"363":{"id":"/using/activity-and-receipts-8","page_id":"/using/activity-and-receipts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/using/activity-and-receipts#outcomes","content":"Held, declined and refused receipts carry the rule that stopped the payment and, for limits, how far over it was."},"364":{"id":"/using/activity-and-receipts-9","page_id":"/using/activity-and-receipts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/using/activity-and-receipts#on-chain","content":"On Stellar testnet, a settled payment emits a `pay` event from the `team-account` contract carrying the spender, service, payee, amount, memo and the spender's spend this period. Settled exceptions emit a `request settled` event. The receipt in the app links to the Stellar transaction so anyone can check it. The replay key passed to `pay` means the same payment cannot be settled twice, even if the app retries."},"365":{"id":"/using/activity-and-receipts-10","page_id":"/using/activity-and-receipts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/using/activity-and-receipts#on-chain","content":"A payment that fails a check never reaches the chain as a transfer, so held, declined and refused receipts are kept by the app; requests and decisions are also recorded as contract events."},"366":{"id":"/using/activity-and-receipts-11","page_id":"/using/activity-and-receipts","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/using/activity-and-receipts#on-chain","content":"The app reads recent contract events from Soroban RPC. A refusal detected before submission is kept only in the current browser and has no transaction link."},"367":{"id":"/using/approvals","page_id":"/using/approvals","type":"page","content":"Approvals","breadcrumbs":["EcoRouter Docs","Using EcoRouter"],"tags":[],"url":"/using/approvals"},"368":{"id":"/using/approvals-0","page_id":"/using/approvals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/using/approvals","content":"Over a limit, a payment is held, not failed, and the owner decides."},"369":{"id":"/using/approvals-1","page_id":"/using/approvals","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/using/approvals#the-flow","content":"The flow"},"370":{"id":"/using/approvals-2","page_id":"/using/approvals","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/using/approvals#what-cannot-be-approved","content":"What cannot be approved"},"371":{"id":"/using/approvals-3","page_id":"/using/approvals","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/using/approvals#agents-do-not-ask","content":"Agents do not ask"},"372":{"id":"/using/approvals-4","page_id":"/using/approvals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/using/approvals","content":"When a person's payment breaks one of four rules, it is **held**: the service is not on their approved list, the amount is over the cap per payment, they have used up their payments for the period, or the amount is over the allowance left. Nothing moves. The payment is not lost either: the spender can ask the owner for an exception to that one payment."},"373":{"id":"/using/approvals-5","page_id":"/using/approvals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/using/approvals#the-flow","content":"**Held.** The spender sees which rule caught the payment and how far over it was, for example `per-payment cap $250 · over by $70`."},"374":{"id":"/using/approvals-6","page_id":"/using/approvals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/using/approvals#the-flow","content":"**Ask for approval.** The spender files a request (`request_approval`). It lands on the owner's **Approvals** screen with the spender, service, amount, memo, the rule that caught it and the overage. The contract also records the service's payee at that moment. Requests expire after 7 days."},"375":{"id":"/using/approvals-7","page_id":"/using/approvals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/using/approvals#the-flow","content":"**Approve or decline.** The owner decides. Declining closes the request and writes a declined receipt."},"376":{"id":"/using/approvals-8","page_id":"/using/approvals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/using/approvals#the-flow","content":"**Settle.** Approving does not move money. Settlement (`settle`) is its own transaction, sent by the owner or by the spender who asked. It refuses if the service's payee changed since the request was filed, and also if the account is paused, the request expired, the service is now unknown or suspended, or the balance is too low. A settled exception does not count against the spender's allowance."},"377":{"id":"/using/approvals-9","page_id":"/using/approvals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/using/approvals#the-flow","content":"Keeping approval and settlement separate means an approval is a decision about one specific payment to one specific payee, not a blank cheque."},"378":{"id":"/using/approvals-10","page_id":"/using/approvals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/using/approvals#what-cannot-be-approved","content":"Some checks cannot be overridden by an approval:"},"379":{"id":"/using/approvals-11","page_id":"/using/approvals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/using/approvals#what-cannot-be-approved","content":"the account or the spender is paused,"},"380":{"id":"/using/approvals-12","page_id":"/using/approvals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/using/approvals#what-cannot-be-approved","content":"the caller is not a spender, or the policy has expired,"},"381":{"id":"/using/approvals-13","page_id":"/using/approvals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/using/approvals#what-cannot-be-approved","content":"the amount is zero or negative,"},"382":{"id":"/using/approvals-14","page_id":"/using/approvals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/using/approvals#what-cannot-be-approved","content":"the replay key was already used,"},"383":{"id":"/using/approvals-15","page_id":"/using/approvals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/using/approvals#what-cannot-be-approved","content":"the service is unknown or suspended in the registry,"},"384":{"id":"/using/approvals-16","page_id":"/using/approvals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/using/approvals#what-cannot-be-approved","content":"the account does not hold enough USDC."},"385":{"id":"/using/approvals-17","page_id":"/using/approvals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/using/approvals#what-cannot-be-approved","content":"These are **refused** outright. Even a request for a service outside the spender's list must name a service the registry resolves; payments never go to a raw address."},"386":{"id":"/using/approvals-18","page_id":"/using/approvals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/using/approvals#agents-do-not-ask","content":"An agent's payment that breaks a limit is refused and stops there. It does not create an approval request. If an agent needs more room, the owner changes its policy. See Agents."},"387":{"id":"/using/assistant","page_id":"/using/assistant","type":"page","content":"Assistant","breadcrumbs":["EcoRouter Docs","Using EcoRouter"],"tags":[],"url":"/using/assistant"},"388":{"id":"/using/assistant-0","page_id":"/using/assistant","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/using/assistant","content":"Ask for a payment in plain words. Five stages check it, and any one can refuse."},"389":{"id":"/using/assistant-1","page_id":"/using/assistant","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/using/assistant#the-five-stages","content":"The five stages"},"390":{"id":"/using/assistant-2","page_id":"/using/assistant","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/using/assistant#why-a-hallucinated-recipient-cannot-happen","content":"Why a hallucinated recipient cannot happen"},"391":{"id":"/using/assistant-3","page_id":"/using/assistant","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/using/assistant#why-the-amount-comes-from-code","content":"Why the amount comes from code"},"392":{"id":"/using/assistant-4","page_id":"/using/assistant","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/using/assistant#what-the-assistant-cannot-do","content":"What the assistant cannot do"},"393":{"id":"/using/assistant-5","page_id":"/using/assistant","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/using/assistant","content":"The **assistant** lets a spender type a sentence such as `top up our inference credits by $120` instead of filling in the payment form. What it produces is a **proposal**. It has no power to pay; the contract still decides."},"394":{"id":"/using/assistant-6","page_id":"/using/assistant","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/using/assistant#the-five-stages","content":"| Stage       | What happens                                         | Refuses when                                           |\n| ----------- | ---------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------ |\n| 1. Sentence | Code, not the model, reads the amount from the text. | There is no amount, or more than one different amount. |","table":"table-0"},"395":{"id":"/using/assistant-7","page_id":"/using/assistant","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/using/assistant#the-five-stages","content":"| Stage        | What happens                                                          | Refuses when                          |\n| ------------ | --------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------- |\n| 2. Assistant | The model picks a service, but only from the spender's approved list. | No approved service fits the request. |","table":"table-0"},"396":{"id":"/using/assistant-8","page_id":"/using/assistant","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/using/assistant#the-five-stages","content":"| Stage     | What happens                                                      | Refuses when                         |\n| --------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------ |\n| 3. Schema | The output must match a fixed shape: `{ service, amount, memo }`. | The output does not match the shape. |","table":"table-0"},"397":{"id":"/using/assistant-9","page_id":"/using/assistant","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/using/assistant#the-five-stages","content":"| Stage       | What happens                                          | Refuses when                    |\n| ----------- | ----------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------- |\n| 4. Registry | The service id must resolve in the on-chain registry. | The id is unknown or suspended. |","table":"table-0"},"398":{"id":"/using/assistant-10","page_id":"/using/assistant","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/using/assistant#the-five-stages","content":"| Stage     | What happens                   | Refuses when                                                             |\n| --------- | ------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| 5. Policy | The full contract policy runs. | A rule fails. A person's limit becomes a hold; anything else is refused. |","table":"table-0"},"399":{"id":"/using/assistant-11","page_id":"/using/assistant","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/using/assistant#why-a-hallucinated-recipient-cannot-happen","content":"The assistant's output shape has **no address field**. The only way to name a destination is a service id, and the only ids it may choose are on the spender's list. An invented address has nowhere to go, and an invented id fails at the registry."},"400":{"id":"/using/assistant-12","page_id":"/using/assistant","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/using/assistant#why-the-amount-comes-from-code","content":"Amounts are read from the sentence by deterministic code and compared with what the model returns. The model cannot change the amount you typed. If the sentence is ambiguous, the request stops at stage 1 and asks you to be specific."},"401":{"id":"/using/assistant-13","page_id":"/using/assistant","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/using/assistant#what-the-assistant-cannot-do","content":"It cannot add services to a list, raise a cap, approve a request or pay an address. Those are owner actions or do not exist at all."},"402":{"id":"/using/make-a-payment","page_id":"/using/make-a-payment","type":"page","content":"Make a payment","breadcrumbs":["EcoRouter Docs","Using EcoRouter"],"tags":[],"url":"/using/make-a-payment"},"403":{"id":"/using/make-a-payment-0","page_id":"/using/make-a-payment","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/using/make-a-payment","content":"Pay a registered service from the team account under a spender policy."},"404":{"id":"/using/make-a-payment-1","page_id":"/using/make-a-payment","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/using/make-a-payment","content":"Open **Pay**, choose a spender, select an approved service and enter a USDC amount. The destination is resolved from the service registry; the payment form does not accept a recipient address."},"405":{"id":"/using/make-a-payment-2","page_id":"/using/make-a-payment","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/using/make-a-payment","content":"Before submitting, the app simulates `check` and shows the contract's verdict. If it passes, the spender signs `pay(spender, service, amount, memo, key)` in Freighter. The team-account contract verifies the policy, resolves the service and transfers USDC to the registered payee."},"406":{"id":"/using/make-a-payment-3","page_id":"/using/make-a-payment","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/using/make-a-payment","content":"After confirmation, **Activity** shows a receipt and an explorer link. A submitted transaction can take time to appear; check its explorer link before retrying."},"407":{"id":"/using/make-a-payment-4","page_id":"/using/make-a-payment","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/using/make-a-payment","content":"Sources: `packages/app/src/screens/Pay.tsx`; `packages/app/src/chain/testnet.ts` (`check`, `pay`); `contracts/team-account/src/lib.rs` (`check`, `pay`)."},"408":{"id":"/using/spenders-and-policies","page_id":"/using/spenders-and-policies","type":"page","content":"Spenders and policies","breadcrumbs":["EcoRouter Docs","Using EcoRouter"],"tags":[],"url":"/using/spenders-and-policies"},"409":{"id":"/using/spenders-and-policies-0","page_id":"/using/spenders-and-policies","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/using/spenders-and-policies","content":"Every person and every agent pays under its own on-chain policy."},"410":{"id":"/using/spenders-and-policies-1","page_id":"/using/spenders-and-policies","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/using/spenders-and-policies#what-a-policy-holds","content":"What a policy holds"},"411":{"id":"/using/spenders-and-policies-2","page_id":"/using/spenders-and-policies","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/using/spenders-and-policies#the-arithmetic","content":"The arithmetic"},"412":{"id":"/using/spenders-and-policies-3","page_id":"/using/spenders-and-policies","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/using/spenders-and-policies#managing-spenders","content":"Managing spenders"},"413":{"id":"/using/spenders-and-policies-4","page_id":"/using/spenders-and-policies","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/using/spenders-and-policies#people-and-agents","content":"People and agents"},"414":{"id":"/using/spenders-and-policies-5","page_id":"/using/spenders-and-policies","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/using/spenders-and-policies","content":"A **spender** is a Stellar address that may pay from the team account: a teammate's wallet or an AI agent's key. Each spender has exactly one **policy**, set by the owner."},"415":{"id":"/using/spenders-and-policies-6","page_id":"/using/spenders-and-policies","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/using/spenders-and-policies#what-a-policy-holds","content":"| Rule | Field  | Example         | What it does                     |\n| ---- | ------ | --------------- | -------------------------------- |\n| Kind | `kind` | Person or Agent | Agents cannot ask for approvals. |","table":"table-0"},"416":{"id":"/using/spenders-and-policies-7","page_id":"/using/spenders-and-policies","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/using/spenders-and-policies#what-a-policy-holds","content":"| Rule  | Field   | Example | What it does    |\n| ----- | ------- | ------- | --------------- |\n| Label | `label` | \"Sam\"   | A display name. |","table":"table-0"},"417":{"id":"/using/spenders-and-policies-8","page_id":"/using/spenders-and-policies","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/using/spenders-and-policies#what-a-policy-holds","content":"| Rule                 | Field       | Example | What it does                             |\n| -------------------- | ----------- | ------- | ---------------------------------------- |\n| Allowance per period | `allowance` | $1,000  | Total the spender may pay in one period. |","table":"table-0"},"418":{"id":"/using/spenders-and-policies-9","page_id":"/using/spenders-and-policies","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/using/spenders-and-policies#what-a-policy-holds","content":"| Rule   | Field    | Example | What it does                                                                           |\n| ------ | -------- | ------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Period | `period` | 30 days | Length of a period. Periods are fixed windows counted from when the spender was added. |","table":"table-0"},"419":{"id":"/using/spenders-and-policies-10","page_id":"/using/spenders-and-policies","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/using/spenders-and-policies#what-a-policy-holds","content":"| Rule            | Field         | Example | What it does                                                    |\n| --------------- | ------------- | ------- | --------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Cap per payment | `max_payment` | $250    | No single payment may be larger. Must not exceed the allowance. |","table":"table-0"},"420":{"id":"/using/spenders-and-policies-11","page_id":"/using/spenders-and-policies","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/using/spenders-and-policies#what-a-policy-holds","content":"| Rule                    | Field          | Example | What it does                                          |\n| ----------------------- | -------------- | ------- | ----------------------------------------------------- |\n| Max payments per period | `max_payments` | 20      | How many payments the spender may make in one period. |","table":"table-0"},"421":{"id":"/using/spenders-and-policies-12","page_id":"/using/spenders-and-policies","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/using/spenders-and-policies#what-a-policy-holds","content":"| Rule   | Field        | Example    | What it does                                            |\n| ------ | ------------ | ---------- | ------------------------------------------------------- |\n| Expiry | `expires_at` | 2026-12-31 | After this time, the policy stops authorizing anything. |","table":"table-0"},"422":{"id":"/using/spenders-and-policies-13","page_id":"/using/spenders-and-policies","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/using/spenders-and-policies#what-a-policy-holds","content":"| Rule              | Field      | Example                           | What it does                                          |\n| ----------------- | ---------- | --------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------- |\n| Approved services | `services` | `inference-credits`, `gpu-rental` | The only service ids this spender may pay (up to 32). |","table":"table-0"},"423":{"id":"/using/spenders-and-policies-14","page_id":"/using/spenders-and-policies","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/using/spenders-and-policies#what-a-policy-holds","content":"| Rule   | Field    | Example | What it does                              |\n| ------ | -------- | ------- | ----------------------------------------- |\n| Paused | `paused` | false   | When true, the spender cannot pay at all. |","table":"table-0"},"424":{"id":"/using/spenders-and-policies-15","page_id":"/using/spenders-and-policies","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/using/spenders-and-policies#what-a-policy-holds","content":"Every limit must be positive. A zero never means \"no limit\"."},"425":{"id":"/using/spenders-and-policies-16","page_id":"/using/spenders-and-policies","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/using/spenders-and-policies#what-a-policy-holds","content":"A policy only ever narrows what a spender can do. There is no rule that lets a spender pay an address directly, and no rule that lets one spender use another's allowance."},"426":{"id":"/using/spenders-and-policies-17","page_id":"/using/spenders-and-policies","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/using/spenders-and-policies#the-arithmetic","content":"The app shows the same arithmetic the contract runs. For a spender with an allowance of $900, $340 already spent and a cap of $250:"},"427":{"id":"/using/spenders-and-policies-18","page_id":"/using/spenders-and-policies","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/using/spenders-and-policies#managing-spenders","content":"**Add** a spender with an address and a policy."},"428":{"id":"/using/spenders-and-policies-19","page_id":"/using/spenders-and-policies","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/using/spenders-and-policies#managing-spenders","content":"**Edit** the policy at any time. Changes apply to the next payment; the current period and its usage are kept."},"429":{"id":"/using/spenders-and-policies-20","page_id":"/using/spenders-and-policies","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/using/spenders-and-policies#managing-spenders","content":"**Pause** a spender to stop them immediately without losing their history. **Resume** to undo."},"430":{"id":"/using/spenders-and-policies-21","page_id":"/using/spenders-and-policies","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/using/spenders-and-policies#managing-spenders","content":"**Remove** a spender to delete their policy. Their address can no longer pay; past receipts stay."},"431":{"id":"/using/spenders-and-policies-22","page_id":"/using/spenders-and-policies","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/using/spenders-and-policies#people-and-agents","content":"Both are spenders and both go through the same checks. The difference is what happens after a payment breaks a limit: a person's payment can become an approval request; an agent's payment is refused and stops there. The contract knows which is which from the policy's `kind`."},"432":{"id":"/using/when-a-payment-is-refused","page_id":"/using/when-a-payment-is-refused","type":"page","content":"When a payment is refused","breadcrumbs":["EcoRouter Docs","Using EcoRouter"],"tags":[],"url":"/using/when-a-payment-is-refused"},"433":{"id":"/using/when-a-payment-is-refused-0","page_id":"/using/when-a-payment-is-refused","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/using/when-a-payment-is-refused","content":"Read the contract rule that stopped a payment and decide what can happen next."},"434":{"id":"/using/when-a-payment-is-refused-1","page_id":"/using/when-a-payment-is-refused","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/using/when-a-payment-is-refused","content":"The team-account contract checks a payment in order and stops at the first failing rule. A refused call does not transfer USDC. The app displays the rule title and, where relevant, the amount over the limit."},"435":{"id":"/using/when-a-payment-is-refused-2","page_id":"/using/when-a-payment-is-refused","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/using/when-a-payment-is-refused","content":"For a person, four policy limits can be sent to the owner as an approval request: service not on the allowlist, per-payment cap, payment count or allowance. Other failures, including a paused account, expired policy, duplicate key, suspended service or insufficient balance, cannot be approved. Agents cannot file approval requests."},"436":{"id":"/using/when-a-payment-is-refused-3","page_id":"/using/when-a-payment-is-refused","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/using/when-a-payment-is-refused","content":"A refusal detected before transaction submission is stored locally in this browser. It is not a contract event and does not have an explorer transaction link. A failure returned by the chain has a transaction result."},"437":{"id":"/using/when-a-payment-is-refused-4","page_id":"/using/when-a-payment-is-refused","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/using/when-a-payment-is-refused","content":"See Error codes, Approvals and Activity and receipts."},"438":{"id":"/using/when-a-payment-is-refused-5","page_id":"/using/when-a-payment-is-refused","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/using/when-a-payment-is-refused","content":"Sources: `packages/app/src/engine/rules.ts`; `packages/app/src/chain/testnet.ts`; `contracts/team-account/src/lib.rs` (`check`, `pay`, `request_approval`)."}},"count":438},"sorting":{"language":"multilingual","sortableProperties":["content","page_id","type","url"],"sortablePropertiesWithTypes":{"content":"string","page_id":"string","type":"string","url":"string"},"sorts":{"content":{"docs":{"1":171,"2":421,"3":188,"4":175,"5":390,"6":227,"7":327,"8":173,"9":186,"10":185,"11":187,"12":369,"13":335,"14":172,"15":252,"16":251,"17":417,"18":240,"19":293,"20":304,"21":386,"22":387,"23":357,"24":19,"25":434,"26":26,"27":415,"28":382,"29":24,"30":130,"31":128,"32":129,"33":25,"34":23,"35":267,"36":324,"37":400,"38":216,"39":318,"40":215,"41":247,"42":402,"43":243,"44":168,"45":317,"46":257,"47":214,"48":149,"49":148,"50":150,"51":151,"52":