125,"264":126,"265":127,"266":355,"267":159,"268":199,"269":160,"270":405,"271":90,"272":92,"273":93,"274":94,"275":91,"276":321,"277":239,"278":350,"279":285,"280":406,"281":62,"282":61,"283":64,"284":63,"285":65,"286":69,"287":67,"288":68,"289":66,"290":109,"291":105,"292":108,"293":106,"294":110,"295":107,"296":426,"297":320,"298":436,"299":418,"300":266,"301":348,"302":313,"303":192,"304":306,"305":305,"306":347,"307":315,"308":352,"309":218,"310":388,"311":376,"312":377,"313":174,"314":291,"315":164,"316":272,"317":379,"318":7,"319":329,"320":259,"321":217,"322":11,"323":17,"324":3,"325":14,"326":0,"327":12,"328":10,"329":8,"330":2,"331":332,"332":307,"333":397,"334":282,"335":410,"336":224,"337":361,"338":162,"339":339,"340":340,"341":290,"342":182,"343":310,"344":300,"345":180,"346":283,"347":181,"348":299,"349":346,"350":416,"351":378,"352":393,"353":326,"354":297,"355":236,"356":275,"357":268,"358":353,"359":103,"360":104,"361":101,"362":102,"363":246,"364":269,"365":155,"366":365,"367":193,"368":276,"369":381,"370":423,"371":176,"372":428,"373":9,"374":5,"375":4,"376":16,"377":258,"378":319,"379":359,"380":373,"381":360,"382":389,"383":391,"384":358,"385":404,"386":189,"387":196,"388":195,"389":380,"390":431,"391":433,"392":425,"393":354,"394":122,"395":120,"396":123,"397":121,"398":124,"399":371,"400":183,"401":256,"402":260,"403":281,"404":273,"405":200,"406":170,"407":336,"408":342,"409":237,"410":420,"411":370,"412":261,"413":287,"414":154,"415":119,"416":118,"417":112,"418":116,"419":114,"420":111,"421":115,"422":113,"423":117,"424":235,"425":156,"426":368,"427":1,"428":6,"429":13,"430":15,"431":202,"432":427,"433":296,"434":396,"435":242,"436":157,"437":308,"438":334},"orderedDocs":[[326,"**Activity history is limited.** The app reads RPC contract events from roughly the last seven days and has no indexer."],[427,"**Add** a spender with an address and a policy."],[330,"**Agent keys are hot keys.** A leaked key can use the spending authority its policy permits until the policy is paused, removed or expires."],[324,"**Agents cannot request approvals.** A refused agent payment cannot be escalated from the app."],[375,"**Approve or decline.** The owner decides. Declining closes the request and writes a declined receipt."],[374,"**Ask for approval.** The spender files a request (`request_approval`). It lands on the owner's **Approvals** screen with the spender, service, amount, memo, the rule that caught it and the overage. The contract also records the service's payee at that moment. Requests expire after 7 days."],[428,"**Edit** the policy at any time. Changes apply to the next payment; the current period and its usage are kept."],[318,"**First write after a deploy is expensive.** The first policy write extended the contract's storage lifetime and charged 368.39 test XLM in fees (transaction cb406cd0…); a simulated policy write now costs about 1 XLM."],[329,"**First write after a deploy is expensive.** The first policy write extended the contract's storage lifetime and charged 368.39 test XLM in fees (transaction cb406cd0…); a simulated policy write now costs about 1 XLM."],[373,"**Held.** The spender sees which rule caught the payment and how far over it was, for example `per-payment cap $250 · over by $70`."],[328,"**No outside merchants are registered.** The five testnet service payees are demo addresses controlled by the deployer."],[322,"**Not audited.** No independent audit has been completed."],[327,"**One worker runs one agent and one service.** Configure another Render worker for another agent/service pair."],[429,"**Pause** a spender to stop them immediately without losing their history. **Resume** to undo."],[325,"**Pre-submission refusals are local.** The app keeps a refusal that never reached the chain only in this browser."],[430,"**Remove** a spender to delete their policy. Their address can no longer pay; past receipts stay."],[376,"**Settle.** Approving does not move money. Settlement (`settle`) is its own transaction, sent by the owner or by the spender who asked. It refuses if the service's payee changed since the request was filed, and also if the account is paused, the request expired, the service is now unknown or suspended, or the balance is too low. A settled exception does not count against the spender's allowance."],[323,"**Testnet only.** The deployed contracts and token are for Stellar testnet."],[125,"`__constructor(owner, asset, registry)` sets the owner, the token contract to pay in (USDC) and the service registry. The account starts unpaused with no spenders."],[24,"`--key` is optional and must be 64 hexadecimal characters when supplied. Reuse the same key to safely retry an unknown result. A caller can parse the JSON line and branch on `status`:"],[161,"`AccountPaused` (1), `UnknownSpender` (2), `SpenderPaused` (3), `PolicyExpired` (4), `InvalidAmount` (5), `ServiceNotAllowed` (6), `DuplicatePayment` (7), `OverPaymentCap` (8), `OverFrequency` (9), `OverAllowance` (10), `UnknownService` (11), `ServiceSuspended` (12), `InsufficientFunds` (13), `InvalidPolicy` (14), `UnknownRequest` (15), `RequestNotPending` (16), `RequestNotApproved` (17), `RequestExpired` (18), `PayeeChanged` (19), `NotAuthorized` (20), `NoExceptionNeeded` (21), `NotEligibleForException` (22), `AgentCannotRequest` (23), `RegistryUnavailable` (24), `NoPendingOwner` (25)."],[153,"`check(spender, service, amount) -> Verdict` runs the same rules without auth or state changes and returns `{ rule, over_by, allowance_left, period_spent, period_count }`. `rule` is `0` when the payment would go through, otherwise the error code that would refuse it. The app uses this to show the arithmetic before anything is signed."],[214,"`check` returns the code for the first failed payment rule. A `pay` call with a failing rule is refused by the contract."],[34,"`pay()` does not resend a transaction automatically. If the result is unknown, call `reconcile(key)`. A safe retry calls `pay()` again with the **same key**. The contract rejects a reused key with rule 7 (`DuplicatePayment`) if the first transaction already paid; `reconcile()` checks `is_key_used` to distinguish that case. Reads, simulations and account-sequence lookups retry network errors up to three times with backoff."],[29,"`PayOutcome` is a discriminated union:"],[33,"`Rule` and `ruleReason` cover the 25 `AccountError` codes. See Error codes."],[26,"`TeamAgent` exposes the public address as `address`; use the same address when the owner creates the agent policy. `teamAccount`, `rpcUrl` and `networkPassphrase` are optional overrides in the constructor."],[154,"`version()`, `owner()`, `asset()`, `registry()`, `paused()`, `balance()`, `spenders()`, `policy(spender) -> Option<Policy>`, `usage(spender) -> Usage`, `request(id) -> Option<ApprovalRequest>`, `requests(from, limit)`, `is_key_used(spender, key)`."],[182,"<Card title=\"Agents\" href=\"/agents/overview\" description=\"Give an agent its own key and policy.\" />"],[183,"<Card title=\"Networks and addresses\" href=\"/reference/networks-and-addresses\" description=\"Find the committed testnet deployments.\" />"],[180,"<Card title=\"Quickstart\" href=\"/getting-started/quickstart\" description=\"Connect Freighter, add testnet funds and make a payment.\" />"],[184,"<Card title=\"Security model\" href=\"/security/security-model\" description=\"Read the contract check order and known risks.\" />"],[181,"<Card title=\"Spenders and policies\" href=\"/using/spenders-and-policies\" description=\"Read the limits stored on each spender.\" />"],[185,"<Card title=\"What we built\" href=\"/resources/what-we-built\" description=\"Source paths, deployed addresses and current limits.\" />"],[210,"| Code | Name                      | Title        |\n| ---- | ------------------------- | ------------ |\n| 22   | `NotEligibleForException` | Not eligible |"],[212,"| Code | Name                  | Title                |\n| ---- | --------------------- | -------------